=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data source (web useTranslation; motorLatest + filteredDrives + toSpeedDisplay +
    speedUnit fed by the parent Driving Dynamics page): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    SpeedGearSource→SpeedGearPanelModel. The view never issues HTTP; the source resolves
    the snapshot + drives + unit prefs and pushes coalesced updates.
  - Composition (web FadeIn > GlassPanel > <h2> + Grid[ShiftTile + 3 metric tiles]):
      • FadeIn      -> TSFadeIn(delay: 0.15) (web `<FadeIn delay={0.15}>`).
      • GlassPanel  -> TSGlassPanel.
      • <h2> title  -> always-visible header, web t('dynamics.speedGear','Speed & Gear').
      • Grid 2/md:4 -> adaptive LazyVGrid (two-up compact, four-up wide).
      • Shift tile  -> big gear letter (motorLatest?.shift_state ?? '—') tinted by
                       shiftColor (D emerald→statusSuccess, R red→statusDanger, N
                       yellow→statusWarning, P muted→textMuted, default→textSecondary)
                       over the "Shift State" badge tinted by shiftBadgeVariant
                       (D success / R danger / N warning / default neutral).
      • Power tile  -> motorLatest?.power_kw != null ? fmtNumber(power_kw) : '—', unit kW
                       (global precision 2).
      • Avg tile    -> avgDriveSpeedMps = drives.len>0 ? mean(avgSpeedMps ?? 0) : null;
                       value = mps!=null ? fmtNumber(toSpeedDisplay(mps),0) : '—', unit
                       speedUnit.
      • Top tile    -> topDriveSpeedMps = drives.len>0 ? max(maxSpeedMps ?? 0) : null;
                       value = mps!=null ? fmtNumber(toSpeedDisplay(mps),0) : '—', unit
                       speedUnit.
      • Double-conversion bug the web source documents: the aggregate is computed ONCE in
        SI and toSpeedDisplay is applied exactly once (at the tile value) — the FIXED
        single-conversion arithmetic, asserted by testSpeedTilesConvertOnceAtZeroDecimals*.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a model/view test):
      loading (skeleton tile grid) · empty (no snapshot AND no drives → friendly
      TSEmptyState, never a blank box) · content (tile grid; per-field '—' for any single
      missing value, web parity) · error (message + Retry; native QueryError affordance) ·
      stale (freshness chip + one guarded auto-refresh) · offline (cached tiles kept +
      offline chip).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved VERBATIM — dynamics.{speedGear, shiftState, power,
      avgDriveSpeed, topDriveSpeed}; native chrome namespaced dynamics.speedGear.* (live/
      stale/offline/updating/loading/empty/errorTitle/retry). Every code-referenced key is
      declared in SpeedGearPanel.strings; referenced==declared VERIFIED (13==13, zero
      orphans). NO English string literals in native code (all via SpeedGearStrings facade
      + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the shift hero, each metric tile, the freshness
      chip, and the Retry button; the grid carries a combined summary ("Shift State D.
      Motor Power 31.40 kW. Avg Drive Speed 30 mph. Top Drive Speed 45 mph"); Dynamic-Type
      system fonts (Font.TS); reduce-motion honored (TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton shimmer).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): SpeedGearPanelModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
      "SpeedGearPanel" exactly once (OSLogSpeedGearTelemetry default; prod app injects the
      shared diagnostics adapter). Asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnce.

